  "interpretation": "Windows surviving Bonferroni (12m, 24m, 36m) and/or BH-FDR only (none) correction, in the biologically expected (negative) direction, indicate a genuine short-to-medium-term effect of chronic heat dose on EC50 beyond the shared trend. Windows that do not survive either correction (48m, 60m) have dose-time collinearity high enough that the detrended residuals are mostly noise, not an independent signal. This is the expected signature of a real but time-limited physiological effect (chronic heat stress integrated over 1-3 years) rather than an artifact of the shared multi-decadal trend, which would not show this decay with window length."
